(60370, 1569, 917, '<td valign="top">If you focused on the near wing, the whole thing would have been in focus.</td>', 'If you focused on the near wing, the whole thing would have been in focus.', '2002-05-15 11:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60371, 1569, 1636, '<td valign="top">Nice,  For a second I thought it was a "real" plane then I saw the size of the grass and realized it was a model</td>', 'Nice,  For a second I thought it was a "real" plane then I saw the size of the grass and realized it was a model', '2002-05-15 12:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60372, 1569, 878, '<td valign="top">Would of been cooler if you could of gotten a shot of the plane flying upsidedown, unless this is the results of it :)</td>', 'Would of been cooler if you could of gotten a shot of the plane flying upsidedown, unless this is the results of it :)', '2002-05-15 13:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60373, 1569, 259, '<td valign="top">definetly upside down</td>', 'definetly upside down', '2002-05-16 00:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60374, 1569, 1, '<td valign="top">Love the idea, as for the shot/angle you''ve chosen, it may be a little bland.  I think a more dramatic angle is needed -- or more props to show that the plane did crash.</td>', 'Love the idea, as for the shot/angle you''ve chosen, it may be a little bland.  I think a more dramatic angle is needed -- or more props to show that the plane did crash.', '2002-05-19 22:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60375, 1569, 749, '<td valign="top">I had hoped that everyone who saw this shot would realise that this is a MODEL aircraft, not a real plane, yet from the comments I can see that little things like the scale of the grass and the very thin landing gear went unnoticed by a couple of you :o)<br/><br/>Yes, this was a set-up shot - I dare not crash this one, since it doesn''t belong to me! I tried various different angles, trying to make it more exciting, and this one was not the best of the bunch. However, I couldn''t use some of the other shots, since there are various background object I had to keep out of shot to hide the fact that this was taken on my back lawn and not on the flying field.<br/><br/>As I said before, this was not my prefered shot, as the focus was on the nose of the plane, rather than the main body, but I was pleased with the lighting - I did some shots later in the day when the sun was brighter, but the glare off the wings was too great...<br/><br/>Thanks for all the comments! :o)</td>', 'I had hoped that everyone who saw this shot would realise that this is a MODEL aircraft, not a real plane, yet from the comments I can see that little things like the scale of the grass and the very thin landing gear went unnoticed by a couple of you :o)Yes, this was a set-up shot - I dare not crash this one, since it doesn''t belong to me! I tried various different angles, trying to make it more exciting, and this one was not the best of the bunch. However, I couldn''t use some of the other shots, since there are various background object I had to keep out of shot to hide the fact that this was taken on my back lawn and not on the flying field.As I said before, this was not my prefered shot, as the focus was on the nose of the plane, rather than the main body, but I was pleased with the lighting - I did some shots later in the day when the sun was brighter, but the glare off the wings was too great...Thanks for all the comments! :o)', '2002-05-26 15:17:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(60376, 1570, 1344, '<td valign="top">Cool pic, but a solid backgroung, some better focus, and cropping of the junk on the right (including the date) would have made it a 10!  Was this like a camcorder vidcap sorta deal?</td>', 'Cool pic, but a solid backgroung, some better focus, and cropping of the junk on the right (including the date) would have made it a 10!  Was this like a camcorder vidcap sorta deal?', '2002-05-13 01:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60377, 1570, 1574, '<td valign="top">Great idea, looks nice...if a little blurry<br/>That date down the bottom-right annoys me greatly</td>', 'Great idea, looks nice...if a little blurryThat date down the bottom-right annoys me greatly', '2002-05-13 02:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60378, 1570, 1360, '<td valign="top">great picture idea, the picture quality could be better, tho.</td>', 'great picture idea, the picture quality could be better, tho.', '2002-05-13 03:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60379, 1570, 1024, '<td valign="top">I am a little disturbed by the date in the lower right corner.  Is there some way to turn that off?  (I did not subtract any points for that, but something you may want to think about).</td>', 'I am a little disturbed by the date in the lower right corner.  Is there some way to turn that off?  (I did not subtract any points for that, but something you may want to think about).', '2002-05-13 08:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60380, 1570, 741, '<td valign="top">[I bet I''m not the only one to say this - can you turn the date imprint off?]<br/>OK ignore that last comment!  2 days later and this shot still sticks in my mind which must mean it''s pretty good!  Thinking about the date, I realise now that it must be deliberate to show that this isn''t just one of those where someone has rotated a perfectly ordinary photo.  Clever idea - it just reminds me too much of all the snaps that I saw ruined by a date stamp when this was popular on film photos.<br/>I really like the way the heights of the glasses are all different which adds a lot of interest to the scene.  However, what lets it down for me is the focusing and (to a lesser extent) the distracting background.  If the glasses had been sharp and the background had been cleaner then I probably would have realised straight away that the trick with the date was a clever idea.</td>', '[I bet I''m not the only one to say this - can you turn the date imprint off?]OK ignore that last comment!  2 days later and this shot still sticks in my mind which must mean it''s pretty good!  Thinking about the date, I realise now that it must be deliberate to show that this isn''t just one of those where someone has rotated a perfectly ordinary photo.  Clever idea - it just reminds me too much of all the snaps that I saw ruined by a date stamp when this was popular on film photos.I really like the way the heights of the glasses are all different which adds a lot of interest to the scene.  However, what lets it down for me is the focusing and (to a lesser extent) the distracting background.  If the glasses had been sharp and the background had been cleaner then I probably would have realised straight away that the trick with the date was a clever idea.', '2002-05-13 11:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60381, 1570, 327, '<td valign="top">Very neat idea here. Looks like they are floating in air.<br/>Out of focus and distraction in the upper right and the lower right (date).<br/>Your on the subject and score for being so creative.</td>', 'Very neat idea here. Looks like they are floating in air.Out of focus and distraction in the upper right and the lower right (date).Your on the subject and score for being so creative.', '2002-05-13 12:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60382, 1570, 737, '<td valign="top">Clever - gains points, but appears out of focus -loses points</td>', 'Clever - gains points, but appears out of focus -loses points', '2002-05-13 12:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60383, 1570, 1128, '<td valign="top">Cool idea, the date stamp is a little distracting...</td>', 'Cool idea, the date stamp is a little distracting...', '2002-05-13 13:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60384, 1570, 772, '<td valign="top">You have a good concept here.  It appears that the glasses are quite a bit out of focus.  Suggestion: Turn your date function off on your camera :)</td>', 'You have a good concept here.  It appears that the glasses are quite a bit out of focus.  Suggestion: Turn your date function off on your camera :)', '2002-05-13 13:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
