(60916, 1606, 885, '<td valign="top">Based on the title, I''m looking for something that''s not ''quite right'' - upside down - in this photo.  The balloons are on the ground, but they might not be helium.  There''s a strange grey band on the bottom of the bottle, that I guess could be air, supported by the fact that the bottle is abnormally full at the top.  It''s certainly not screaming "upside-down" to me.  I may be dense, but I admit that I''m missing it.  I''m guessing that it''s actually really upside-down and glued down then flipped?Otherwise though, a very nice photo, minor distractions with the glare on the surface of the table.</td>', 'Based on the title, I''m looking for something that''s not ''quite right'' - upside down - in this photo.  The balloons are on the ground, but they might not be helium.  There''s a strange grey band on the bottom of the bottle, that I guess could be air, supported by the fact that the bottle is abnormally full at the top.  It''s certainly not screaming "upside-down" to me.  I may be dense, but I admit that I''m missing it.  I''m guessing that it''s actually really upside-down and glued down then flipped?Otherwise though, a very nice photo, minor distractions with the glare on the surface of the table.', '2002-05-14 08:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60917, 1606, 862, '<td valign="top">How did you do that?  Is everything glued upside down?</td>', 'How did you do that?  Is everything glued upside down?', '2002-05-14 12:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60918, 1606, 139, '<td valign="top">I really enjoyed this photo.  It was Escheresque to me in that, at first glance, I think I see the entire photo, and then, after looking for a few moments, the reality of the photo hits me, and I realize that all of my assumptions were wrong.  Great job, and excellent subtlety.</td>', 'I really enjoyed this photo.  It was Escheresque to me in that, at first glance, I think I see the entire photo, and then, after looking for a few moments, the reality of the photo hits me, and I realize that all of my assumptions were wrong.  Great job, and excellent subtlety.', '2002-05-14 13:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60919, 1606, 107, '<td valign="top">I''m struggling to find the upside-downess (did I just invent a word?) of this shot.  Perhaps when I come back and have a second or third look.  Regardless, it''s a fantastic photograph.</td>', 'I''m struggling to find the upside-downess (did I just invent a word?) of this shot.  Perhaps when I come back and have a second or third look.  Regardless, it''s a fantastic photograph.', '2002-05-15 09:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60920, 1606, 1570, '<td valign="top">oh, now i get it! it''s good.</td>', 'oh, now i get it! it''s good.', '2002-05-15 09:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
