(60937, 1606, 449, '<td valign="top">I dont believe the ad min note. How on earth is this relative to the upside down challenge and not the advertisement challenge? The balloons in the bottle?</td>', 'I dont believe the ad min note. How on earth is this relative to the upside down challenge and not the advertisement challenge? The balloons in the bottle?', '2002-05-19 23:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60938, 1606, 527, '<td valign="top">This is clearly very well done but I''m not clear on why it was done other than the fact that you could. Especially when it looks so normal that it required a disclaimer on it. Other than the drip at the tip of the straw I wish there was something else happening that looks impossible.</td>', 'This is clearly very well done but I''m not clear on why it was done other than the fact that you could. Especially when it looks so normal that it required a disclaimer on it. Other than the drip at the tip of the straw I wish there was something else happening that looks impossible.', '2002-05-19 23:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60939, 1606, 1078, '<td valign="top">A couple of quick comments.<br/><br/>The light portion in the middle of the shot appears to be a lens flair of some kind.  The reason it didn''t get "fixed" is actually pretty simple: on my computer at home, it''s not there.  This is yet another of those monitor calibration problems.  I believe my monitor is calibrated correctly using Adobe Gamma, but I may be wrong -- or maybe it''s yours...  Secondly, after having it pointed out, I tried to fix it using levels, and I don''t think it''s possible without radically altering the other colors.  If someone would like to show me I''m wrong, I''d very much like to learn because I don''t know how.<br/><br/>A number of people mentioned using less soda.  I could have, but I didn''t want it to be blatantly obvious.  Besides, I have the feeling that if I had used less, I would have had people telling me I should have used more.<br/><br/>Subtlety was also a comment made by a number of people.  Some thought it was too much and some thought it was great.  My goal was not to make this easy to see.  I hoped that knowing it was upside down, people would take an initial look, not see what was upside down, and look harder.  I do that with photos when I can''t see the challenge aspect -- in fact, I probably spend more time looking at photos I don''t get than photos I do.  I was also realistic, though, and didn''t expect everybody to see it -- and I was OK with that.<br/><br/>Finally, maybe I should have used a different kind of soda.  I think some of the people who couldn''t see the upside down were unable to because they thought the air bubble at the bottom of the bottle was the "cream" portion of the soda.<br/><br/>For those of you who recognized this as an ad shot, it is.  It just happens to be upside down as well.<br/><br/></td>', 'A couple of quick comments.The light portion in the middle of the shot appears to be a lens flair of some kind.  The reason it didn''t get "fixed" is actually pretty simple: on my computer at home, it''s not there.  This is yet another of those monitor calibration problems.  I believe my monitor is calibrated correctly using Adobe Gamma, but I may be wrong -- or maybe it''s yours...  Secondly, after having it pointed out, I tried to fix it using levels, and I don''t think it''s possible without radically altering the other colors.  If someone would like to show me I''m wrong, I''d very much like to learn because I don''t know how.A number of people mentioned using less soda.  I could have, but I didn''t want it to be blatantly obvious.  Besides, I have the feeling that if I had used less, I would have had people telling me I should have used more.Subtlety was also a comment made by a number of people.  Some thought it was too much and some thought it was great.  My goal was not to make this easy to see.  I hoped that knowing it was upside down, people would take an initial look, not see what was upside down, and look harder.  I do that with photos when I can''t see the challenge aspect -- in fact, I probably spend more time looking at photos I don''t get than photos I do.  I was also realistic, though, and didn''t expect everybody to see it -- and I was OK with that.Finally, maybe I should have used a different kind of soda.  I think some of the people who couldn''t see the upside down were unable to because they thought the air bubble at the bottom of the bottle was the "cream" portion of the soda.For those of you who recognized this as an ad shot, it is.  It just happens to be upside down as well.', '2002-05-20 09:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(60940, 1606, 1042, '<td valign="top">I really can''t believe that so many people looked at this and still didn''t realize it was upside down. How much time do you think people are really taking to look if they couldn''t see? Personally, I thought it was a very clever and unique idea and I''m guessing you would have scored so much better if folks would have just "gotten" the whole thing. And no, I didn''t comment.....I''m trying to get better with that...I worked overtime that week every night. Excuses, excuses...but I hope it''s not too late to compliment the fine job you did and the excellent way you chose to present the challenge to us.</td>', 'I really can''t believe that so many people looked at this and still didn''t realize it was upside down. How much time do you think people are really taking to look if they couldn''t see? Personally, I thought it was a very clever and unique idea and I''m guessing you would have scored so much better if folks would have just "gotten" the whole thing. And no, I didn''t comment.....I''m trying to get better with that...I worked overtime that week every night. Excuses, excuses...but I hope it''s not too late to compliment the fine job you did and the excellent way you chose to present the challenge to us.', '2002-05-22 21:15:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(60941, 1608, 1024, '<td valign="top">Very very nice.</td>', 'Very very nice.', '2002-05-13 08:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60942, 1608, 1037, '<td valign="top">This is a very pretty setting, and I like the vertical cropping. I think though that turning this one upside down was overkill, when the reflection itself would have been fine (I think), and this just makes it confusing (to me, anyway). Some photos of reflections in this challenge have been really enhanced by turning them upside down, perhaps because they were planned that way, but this one doesn''t seem to work to me.</td>', 'This is a very pretty setting, and I like the vertical cropping. I think though that turning this one upside down was overkill, when the reflection itself would have been fine (I think), and this just makes it confusing (to me, anyway). Some photos of reflections in this challenge have been really enhanced by turning them upside down, perhaps because they were planned that way, but this one doesn''t seem to work to me.', '2002-05-13 08:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60943, 1608, 1175, '<td valign="top">I think you may have gone just a tad too far on the whole upside down thing.  Just taking a picture of the reflection would have been nice.  I would also have moved the horizon down to the the rule of 3rds line.</td>', 'I think you may have gone just a tad too far on the whole upside down thing.  Just taking a picture of the reflection would have been nice.  I would also have moved the horizon down to the the rule of 3rds line.', '2002-05-13 11:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60944, 1608, 327, '<td valign="top">Hey,  pretty place. Right on the subject of the challenge.<br/>Good idea, nice work.</td>', 'Hey,  pretty place. Right on the subject of the challenge.Good idea, nice work.', '2002-05-13 12:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60945, 1608, 772, '<td valign="top">Good shot!  Looks like the camera is upside down on this one... I like it!</td>', 'Good shot!  Looks like the camera is upside down on this one... I like it!', '2002-05-13 14:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60946, 1608, 885, '<td valign="top">Kind of disconcerting how the reflection is on top.  Possible because that water is so still.</td>', 'Kind of disconcerting how the reflection is on top.  Possible because that water is so still.', '2002-05-13 14:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(60947, 1608, 1226, '<td valign="top">You can barely see the waterline... it fools the eye. Very nice.</td>', 'You can barely see the waterline... it fools the eye. Very nice.', '2002-05-13 19:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
